IMPORT prelude

-- Privy Council (Appeals from the High Court) Act 1975 (Cth) — THE NOUNS,
-- RULE AND TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00255.txt.
-- Seat: the litigant.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `High Court decision` HAS
    -- s 3: special leave "could, but for this Act, have been asked in
    -- accordance with section 3 of the Privy Council (Limitations of
    -- Appeals) Act 1968-1973"
    `special leave was open under the 1968 Act`         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 3: "unless the decision ... was given in a proceeding that was
    -- commenced in a court before the date of commencement of this Act"
    `the proceeding began before this Act commenced`    IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Rule`

@ref s 3
@export default Does s 3 of the Privy Council (Appeals from the High Court) Act 1975 (Cth) leave open my asking Her Majesty in Council for special leave to appeal from this High Court decision? Where special leave was open under s 3 of the Privy Council (Limitation of Appeals) Act 1968, it is barred unless the proceeding began in a court before this Act commenced (TRUE means not barred). NOTHING where special leave was not open under the 1968 Act, which this Act does not change. DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN h IS A `High Court decision`  @desc Whether special leave was open under the 1968 Act, and when the proceeding began
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`may I still ask for special leave from` h MEANS
    IF h's `special leave was open under the 1968 Act`
    THEN JUST (h's `the proceeding began before this Act commenced`)
    ELSE NOTHING
